@* Decision 0011 (run W3, unit AP): the mockup's _AppearancePreview: a sample exchange in the chat's own message markup (_ChatItem's user
   bubble, thinking block, tool card, code block and usage footer), so every setting shows as it will in a chat. It is marked as a sample
   and holds no measured number: the footer names its fields instead. appearance.js sets the form's unsaved values on it (data-density,
   data-code-theme, data-code-ligatures, data-usage-footer, data-user-markdown, data-reduce-motion; the font size as a zoom; the thinking and tool cards open or
   closed); the page's global settings never apply to it (appearance.css and appearance.js skip [data-appearance-preview]). The sample
   reply names the default model when one is set. Model: AppearancePage. *@
@using PiSharp.WebAgent.Appearance
@model AppearancePage
<div class="ps-card ap-preview" id="livePreview" data-appearance-preview data-density="comfortable" data-code-theme="default" data-code-ligatures="off"
     data-usage-footer="on" data-user-markdown="off" data-reduce-motion="off">
  <div class="ap-preview-head d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 border-bottom fs-8 text-ps-faint">
    <span class="ps-chip" data-tone="outline">sample</span><span>Example text, not a chat of yours.</span>
  </div>
  <div class="p-3 ap-preview-scale" data-preview-scale>
    <article class="msg msg-user">
      <div class="msg-body">
        <div class="msg-content msg-plain" data-user-md>Add a **null check** to `CacheStats.Merge` and run the tests.</div>
        <div class="msg-content msg-user-md"><p>Add a <strong>null check</strong> to <code>CacheStats.Merge</code> and run the tests.</p></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="msg msg-assistant mb-0">
      <div class="msg-body">
        <div class="msg-role"><span class="msg-model">@(Model.SampleModel ?? "PiSharp")</span></div>
        <details class="thinking" data-preview-detail="expandThinking">
          <summary><i class="bi bi-chevron-right"></i><i class="bi bi-lightbulb"></i> Thinking</summary>
          <div class="thinking-body">Merge reads other.Buckets without a guard. A null other should throw ArgumentNullException, as the other public methods do.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="tool-card" data-preview-detail="expandToolCalls">
          <summary>
            <span class="tool-icon"><i class="bi bi-pencil-square"></i></span>
            <span class="tool-name">edit</span>
            <span class="tool-args-summary">src/PiSharp.AI/CacheStats.cs · 1 edit</span>
            <span class="ps-chip" data-tone="ok">done</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="tool-body"><div class="ps-term"><pre class="wrap"><code>@@@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@@@
 public CacheStats Merge(CacheStats other)
 {
+    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(other);</code></pre></div></div>
        </details>
        <div class="msg-content">
          <p>Added the guard. <code>Merge</code> now throws for a null argument, like the rest of the type:</p>
          <div class="ps-term">
            <div class="ps-term-bar"><span class="dot"></span>CacheStats.cs</div>
            <pre><code>public CacheStats Merge(CacheStats other)
{
    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(other);
    var hits = Hits + other.Hits;
    return hits >= 0 &amp;&amp; other != Empty ? new(hits, Misses + other.Misses) : this;
}
public bool IsEmpty => Hits == 0;</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p class="stream-cursor mb-0">The sample stops here</p>
        </div>
        <div class="msg-footer pv-usage">
          <span><i class="bi bi-arrow-up"></i>input tokens</span>
          <span><i class="bi bi-arrow-down"></i>output tokens</span>
          <span><i class="bi bi-lightning-charge"></i>cached</span>
          <span>cost</span>
          <span><i class="bi bi-stopwatch"></i>duration</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
